# LaTeX build artifacts
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
paper/_build/

# Regenerated publication artefacts (WP-037). `paper/main.tex` and
# `paper/supplementary.tex` are tracked sources; the figures and tables they
# \includegraphics / \input are derived output, regenerated byte-comparably by
# `python tools/reproduce.py --output-dir paper` from the manifest-governed
# stored JSON artefacts. Tracking them would make generated binaries both an
# output and a source, and would churn on every regeneration — the same
# reasoning that keeps DOCS/test_and_benchmark_results/ ignored below.
paper/figures/*.pdf
paper/figures/*.png
paper/tables/tab_*.tex

# Model weights (large files)
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth
!models/subconscious_controller.onnx
!models/subconscious_controller.onnx.data

# Docs build
DOCS/sphinx/_build/
# Nested build directory used by the ported acceptance test
# tests/test_acceptance_y4q3.py::TestSphinxDocs::test_sphinx_build_succeeds.
DOCS/sphinx/_build_test/

# Generated benchmark reports/artefacts (canonical artefacts live in benchmarks/results/)
DOCS/test_and_benchmark_results/

# Benchmark-run side-effects written into the (otherwise-tracked, currently-empty)
# results dir by ported acceptance tests — e.g. test_acceptance_y4q1_9.py's
# `bench_preregistration()` `_save("preregistration_hash", ...)` (WP036C-F7).
# Real campaign artefacts are added deliberately at WP-038, not left by a test run.
benchmarks/results/*_preregistration_hash.json

# Archived reference material is tracked but never imported at runtime
# (DOCS/archive and reference from PRINet 3.0/ is reference-only)
